Changing the frame of a usd procedural in an interactive session updates it without regenerating it

When the hydra translation is used, the usd stage is kept in memory during interactive sessions,
so that a frame change only syncs the time-varying primitives. The arnold nodes of the 
non-animated primitives must be preserved. In the legacy usd translation, the procedural 
contents are regenerated.

See #2422

author: sebastien.ortega
